hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1122","Chapter on hastening the division of spoils near the enemy, 1161 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dividing the spoils at al-Ji'ranah when a man stood and said: Be just, for you have not been just. He said: Woe to you; who will be just if I am not just? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: Leave him, for this one has companions - or: is among companions - who recite the Qur'an without it passing their throats; they pass out of religion as an arrow passes out of the game."
